>what does it mean when se is place between brivla?

se always converts the next brivla.

>i thought it is not legal but the doc says otherwise. If i say

>  mi sutra klama do

>with the use of se it would be

>  do se sutra klama mi

No, actually. It would be do sutra se klama mi. se sutra klama parses as
((se sutra) klama) mi, and is thus a form of klamaing rather than of se
klamaing.

Now we just need somebody to rewrite that in words that make sense, because
